Subject: [PATCH 0001] aerial-fh: size the GPU comm send-peer table for the cells actually configured

kGpuCommSendPeers defaults to API_MAX_NUM_CELLS, a compile-time constant that is
16, 32 or 64 depending on the build. It is one of three factors in the fronthaul
packet buffer:

    nic.cpp:984   num_packets = kGpuCommSendPeers * kMaxFlows * kMaxPktsFlow
                              = 32 * 32 * 2048        (in a 20-cell build)

The buffer is therefore sized for the maximum cell count the binary was compiled
for, not for the cells a given deployment actually configures. On a single-cell
4T4R 100 MHz deployment this reserves roughly 16 GiB of GPU memory, about two
thirds of the process footprint, of which the great majority is never addressed.

Fixing the constant at 4 sizes the table for a small-cell-count deployment.
Measured on one 4T4R 100 MHz cell at full F08 load, combined with mtu 2048 and
max_harq_pools 64 in the controller YAML:

    footprint   24,747 MiB  ->  4,955 MiB
    throughput  1,369.97 Mbps down / 498.22 up, unchanged
    CRC errors  0, unchanged
    DL U-plane prepare  25.6 us -> 13.1 us   (the stage walks the peer table)

Downlink U-plane prepare roughly halves, because that stage iterates the peer
table; a shorter table is less work per slot. No stage got slower.

This is a deployment-sizing change, not a fix. 4 is correct only while the
deployment configures at most 4 cells. A cleaner form would read the value from
the controller YAML alongside cell_group_num rather than hard-coding it, which
would remove the rebuild; that is left for a later patch.

--- a/cuPHY-CP/aerial-fh-driver/lib/defaults.hpp
+++ b/cuPHY-CP/aerial-fh-driver/lib/defaults.hpp
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
  * See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
  * limitations under the License.
  */
+
+/*
+ * NOTICE: modified from the NVIDIA Aerial CUDA-Accelerated RAN SDK 26-1-cubb.
+ * Change: kGpuCommSendPeers fixed at 4 instead of API_MAX_NUM_CELLS.
+ * Marked as required by Apache License 2.0 section 4(b).
+ */
 
 #ifndef AERIAL_FH_DEFAULTS_HPP__
 #define AERIAL_FH_DEFAULTS_HPP__
@@ -81,7 +87,7 @@
 constexpr uint32_t THREAD_PER_PACKET_COPY = 8;               //!< Threads per packet copy operation
 constexpr uint32_t kThreadSymbol = 16;                       //!< Threads per symbol
 constexpr uint32_t kPeerSymbolPrbBox = 16 * 32;              //!< PRB boxes per symbol (16 AP × 32 boxes)
-constexpr uint32_t kGpuCommSendPeers = API_MAX_NUM_CELLS;    //!< Max GPU comm send peers (cells)
+constexpr uint32_t kGpuCommSendPeers = 4;                    //!< Max GPU comm send peers (cells)
 
 // PRB split info size
 constexpr uint32_t kPrbSplitInfo = kPeerSlotsInfo * kPeerSymbolsInfo * 32 * 273;  //!< Total PRB split info entries
